\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textsc  {Directed}\xspace  's decisions by change family (Sonnet- and Haiku-built programs, main test sets). Pairs: all program--question pairs. Wrong: wrong answers with no added check. Kept: wrong answers \textsc  {Directed}\xspace  trusts. Declines are split into those that \emph  {detect} (\textsf  {Caught}\xspace  , \textsf  {Already caught}\xspace  , \textsf  {Failed history check}\xspace  ) and those that \emph  {abstain} (\textsf  {Untestable}\xspace  , \textsf  {Can't express}\xspace  , \textsf  {Request rejected}\xspace  ), each as wrong answers removed / correct answers lost. No-effect controls are also counted in their families.}}{8}{table.caption.33}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:families}{{5}{8}{\gate 's decisions by change family (Sonnet- and Haiku-built programs, main test sets). Pairs: all program--question pairs. Wrong: wrong answers with no added check. Kept: wrong answers \gate trusts. Declines are split into those that \emph {detect} (\Caught , \Already , \Failhist ) and those that \emph {abstain} (\Untestable , \Cantexpress , \Badrequest ), each as wrong answers removed / correct answers lost. No-effect controls are also counted in their families}{table.caption.33}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Policy reuse (Sonnet- and Haiku-built workflow programs; 683 P and 728 H pairs from 31 programs). Each program starts from its capability record at the end of the test runs. P adds one worker to one pool; H rewords the rules without changing them. No P or H document has the policy fingerprint of a test document, so no test result applied to any of these pairs. Exec.: program executions per pair beyond the factual and answer runs.}}{8}{table.caption.35}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:reuse}{{6}{8}{Policy reuse (Sonnet- and Haiku-built workflow programs; 683 P and 728 H pairs from 31 programs). Each program starts from its capability record at the end of the test runs. P adds one worker to one pool; H rewords the rules without changing them. No P or H document has the policy fingerprint of a test document, so no test result applied to any of these pairs. Exec.: program executions per pair beyond the factual and answer runs}{table.caption.35}{}}
